.TH SMOOTH_T 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
smooth_t \- Framerate\-independent smoothing: the fraction of the remaining distance to move toward a target this tick, given a time constant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqmathx.h\(dq
.BI "float smooth_t(float smoothing, float dt);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Framerate\-independent smoothing: the fraction of the remaining distance to move toward a target this tick, given a time constant. value = lerpf(value, target, smooth_t(0.2f, dt)) approaches target with the same feel at any tick rate, reaching about 63% of the way in `smoothing` seconds. 0 or negative smoothing snaps (returns 1). camera_follow() is built on it.
.PP
This is a static inline function; it is defined in the header.
.SH RETURN VALUE
a fraction in 0..1.
.SH MODULE
math (src/engine/math/mathx.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lerpf (3),
.BR v2_lerp (3),
.BR camera_follow (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
